                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "85244e7c-29d1-4829-af4b-1ac412ef2699",
                                "sense_id": "1ae687af-b2ca-3b31-ae26-a7c65fb18948",
                                "text": "Izrael zaapelował do świata o przeszkodzenie irańskiemu planowi nuklearnemu."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cf3c286c-868f-4b85-99ca-9773dc954a23",
                        "source_entry_id": "a6766da1-c246-337b-8894-c8c7d6e500ad",
                        "source_sense_id": "1ae687af-b2ca-3b31-ae26-a7c65fb18948",
                        "target_lang_word": "prevention",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "prevention",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "337f8248-467e-3cb4-a7fb-fd1613511a27",
                                        "entry_id": "e75aed6e-ef3f-361f-8774-b73a84063d3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of preventing or hindering; obstruction of action, access, or approach; thwarting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "688c6d62-d78c-4c5d-b361-da5acd0c7eb9",
                                                "sense_id": "337f8248-467e-3cb4-a7fb-fd1613511a27",
                                                "text": "a fire prevention campaign"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f35f3b7a-c3b3-4733-8864-9c462b5c16ee",
                                                "sense_id": "337f8248-467e-3cb4-a7fb-fd1613511a27",
                                                "text": "Casca, be sudden, for we fear prevention."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62f5da6c-7ece-4e1a-9adb-cd0570959741",
                                                "sense_id": "337f8248-467e-3cb4-a7fb-fd1613511a27",
                                                "text": "But no Man Pities another for any Evil lying upon Him, which he would not help, but which he could not. One is his Burden, the other his Choice; Vertually at least, since he might have Chosen its Prevention."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "636127f0-dc4a-4c10-9195-6e8a272802a6",
                                                "sense_id": "337f8248-467e-3cb4-a7fb-fd1613511a27",
                                                "text": "It performed this task in the beginning and has always exercised the power of passing on books. By this transfer, the Pope points out, every danger of a collision, which might become very embarrassing, is evaded. The prevention of such collisions has indeed been one of the chief reasons for Pius X to undertake the complete reorganization of the Roman Curia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51eb534b-2502-4a3a-bedd-dace44b80414",
                                                "sense_id": "337f8248-467e-3cb4-a7fb-fd1613511a27",
                                                "text": "In the next few days we'll announce the administration's new strategy for the prevention of drug abuse and drug trafficking."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d44535e8-44be-3e04-9b6b-19081d7b7a06",
                                        "entry_id": "e75aed6e-ef3f-361f-8774-b73a84063d3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any measure intended to limit health-related risks (such as information campaigns, vaccination, early diagnosis etc.)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6fdd417e-c570-4f66-98ca-0a06aa531ac8",
                                                "sense_id": "d44535e8-44be-3e04-9b6b-19081d7b7a06",
                                                "text": "Whatever cures are known, and preventions that are practiced now, could have been common knowledge centuries ago."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "30b43f3d-1773-39a5-8a5f-4740c0031c91",
                                        "entry_id": "e75aed6e-ef3f-361f-8774-b73a84063d3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of going, or state of being, before."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2b70473-5864-4380-a792-303204c8d109",
                                                "sense_id": "30b43f3d-1773-39a5-8a5f-4740c0031c91",
                                                "text": "It is generally knowne and obserued, that Light, and the Obiect of Sight, moue swifter than Sound; For we see the Flash of a Peece [i.e. firearm] is seene sooner, than the Noise is heard. […] And the greater the Distance, the greater is the Preuention: As we see in Thunder, which is farre off; where the Lightning Precedeth the Cracke a good space."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c4388b2-d359-3853-9476-12bbe2c63e86",
                                        "entry_id": "e75aed6e-ef3f-361f-8774-b73a84063d3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anticipation; especially, anticipation of needs, wishes, hazards and risks"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7995116-06fd-4922-a232-498829710bb5",
                                                "sense_id": "7c4388b2-d359-3853-9476-12bbe2c63e86",
                                                "text": "[Suffolk, York and Beaufort]\nHave all limed bushes to betray thy wings,\nAnd, fly thou how thou canst, they’ll tangle thee:\nBut fear not thou, until thy foot be snared,\nNor never seek prevention of thy foes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "831b62d4-b018-319b-b39d-2dd14620baa8",
                                        "entry_id": "e75aed6e-ef3f-361f-8774-b73a84063d3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "precaution; forethought."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8659cead-9231-4735-aeed-3d2f680a6a05",
                                                "sense_id": "831b62d4-b018-319b-b39d-2dd14620baa8",
                                                "text": "1659, Henry Hammond, A Paraphrase and Annotations upon All the Books of the New Testament, London: Richard Davis, The Gospel according to S. LUKE, Chapter 14, verse 3, p. 238,\nAnd Jesus […] by way of prevention asked a question of the Doctors of the law and Pharisees that were present, saying, Is the working of a cure on a sick man a thing forbidden, and so unlawfull to be done upon a sabbath day?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ed731b41-b587-48dd-b1a7-b941e7a38f34",
                        "source_entry_id": "a6766da1-c246-337b-8894-c8c7d6e500ad",
                        "source_sense_id": "1ae687af-b2ca-3b31-ae26-a7c65fb18948",
                        "target_lang_word": "interruption",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "interruption",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c8d0973-850f-35a9-9aba-0c950c7a5f55",
                                        "entry_id": "039eb0d1-5c02-3f3d-890e-b3357b55d7ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of interrupting, or the state of being interrupted."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b572bdc-47fd-4048-b843-20ae0ca8421f",
                                                "sense_id": "2c8d0973-850f-35a9-9aba-0c950c7a5f55",
                                                "text": "One morning I had been driven to the precarious refuge afforded by the steps of the inn, after rejecting offers from the Celebrity to join him in a variety of amusements. But even here I was not free from interruption, for he was seated on a horse-block below me, playing with a fox terrier."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "100263b3-3732-4ebc-b265-c0f729e1517a",
                                                "sense_id": "2c8d0973-850f-35a9-9aba-0c950c7a5f55",
                                                "text": "The dirty secret of the internet is that all this distraction and interruption is immensely profitable. Web companies like to boast about \"creating compelling content\", or offering services that let you \"stay up to date with what your friends are doing\"[…]and so on."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a432b529-7d09-3c77-85ce-c5a568c42462",
                                        "entry_id": "039eb0d1-5c02-3f3d-890e-b3357b55d7ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "the act of breaking into someone else’s speech."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2abe068d-54b3-370d-b16e-1a4989518087",
                                        "entry_id": "039eb0d1-5c02-3f3d-890e-b3357b55d7ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A time interval during which there is a cessation of something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
